hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22832","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Amr ash-Shaybani, who said: Riyah as-Suhaymi came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: My children and my wealth were raided. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for the wealth, it has been divided, and as for the children, go with him, O Bilal, and if he recognizes his child, hand him over to him. He said: So he went with him and showed him to him, and he said: Do you recognize him? He said: Yes. So he handed him over, and he went to him. Sufyan said: They think he had accepted Islam before he was raided."
"22833","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from ash-Shabi, from Riyah as-Suhaymi, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote to him on a red leather, so he took the book of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and patched his bucket with it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent a detachment, and they left for him no grazing nor pasturing animal, nor family nor wealth, except they took it. And he escaped naked upon a horse of his with no saddle upon it, until he came to his daughter, and she was married among Banu Hilal, and she had accepted Islam and her family had accepted Islam. And the gathering place of the people was in the courtyard of her house, so he went around until he entered upon her from behind the house. He said: So when she saw him she threw a garment over him. She said: What is with you? He said: All evil has befallen your father; nothing was left for him, neither grazing nor pasturing animal, nor family nor wealth, except it was taken. She said: You were called to Islam. He said: Where is your husband? She said: Among the camels. He said: So he went to him and said: What is with you? He said: All evil has befallen him; nothing was left for him, neither grazing nor pasturing animal, nor family nor wealth, except it was taken, and I want Muhammad, hastening to him before he divides my family and my wealth. He said: So take my mount with its saddle. He said: I have no need of it in it. He said: So he took the shepherd's young camel and provisioned him a waterskin of water. He said: And upon him was a garment, when he covered his face with it his buttocks came out, and when he covered his buttocks his face came out, and he disliked being recognized, until he reached Medina. So he tied his mount, then came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and was beside him where he prayed. So when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Fajr, he said: O Messenger of Allah, stretch your hands that I may pledge you. So he stretched it, and when he wanted to strike upon it, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, withheld it to himself. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did that three times, withholding it to himself, and he would do it. So when it was the third time, he said: Who are you? He said: Riyah as-Suhaymi. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took his upper arm, then raised it, then said: O company of Muslims, this is Riyah as-Suhaymi, to whom I wrote and he took my book and patched his bucket with it. So he began pleading to him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, my family and my wealth. He said: As for your wealth, it has been divided, and as for your family, whoever you are able to overpower of them. So he went out, and his son had recognized the mount while standing at it. So he returned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: This is my son. So he said: O Bilal, go out with him and ask him: Is this your father? If he says yes, hand him to him. So Bilal went out to him and said: Is this your father? He said: Yes. So he returned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I never saw anyone weep to his companion. So he said: That is the harshness of the Bedouins."
